# Sync frontend docs with the server repo

Whenever this frontend changes (feature, bug fix, screen, route, copy, or live URL), update **`README.md` and screenshots in this repo and the matching files in the server repo** in the same effort. Keep both sides aligned.

## Same change must cover

- `README.md` — short project description at the top, live URLs, tech stack, screens, features
- `docs/screenshots/auth|admin|user/` — every portal screen
- `docs/screenshots/live/` — API status, health, Swagger (copied from capture)
- Server sibling: `../server/README.md` (shared blurb + URLs) and `../server/docs/screenshots/` (same screenshot tree)

If a new screen or route is added, add it to the README **and** to `scripts/capture-screens.mjs`, then recapture:

```bash
node scripts/capture-screens.mjs
```

## Do not

- Do not invent features that are not in the code
- Do not commit secrets
- Do not update only this README when screens or shared product text changed
- Do not uncomment Cursor-rule notes in README (keep them HTML-commented)
